# Always push and deploy

After finishing product/code changes the user would expect on the live site:

1. **Commit** (HEREDOC message; no secrets; follow git safety rules)
2. **Push** to `origin` (usually `main`)
3. **Deploy** to production droplet `root@167.71.217.5`, app at `/var/www/zei`, pm2 process `zei`:
   - `git fetch && git reset --hard origin/main`
   - `npm ci && npm run build`
   - `pm2 restart zei --update-env`
   - Fix corrupted `node_modules`/npm cache if build fails, then rebuild
4. Verify HTTP 200 on the droplet (or https://cryptozei.com / www)

Do this by default — do not leave finished work “local only” unless the user explicitly says not to deploy (e.g. experiment-only).
